On Wed, Dec 04, 2002 at 01:25:51PM +0100, Xavier Grave wrote:
> Hi,
> 
> As far as I can see there is a sound output from my mother board. But I don't 
> see any entry in /proc/pci or have any answer from pnpdump.
> 
> Does anybody know how to find and configure the sound on this kind of
> machine ?

I have the following in /etc/modutils/sound:

# Sound - copied from Debian list
options sb esstype=1868 io=0x220 irq=5 dma=1 dma16=5 mpu_io=0x320
post-install sb /usr/bin/aumix -L
alias sound-slot-0 sb
alias sound-service-0-3 sb
alias sound sb

-- 

patrick



